s we look to the future, realizing a robust financial sustainability model is a critical part of ensuring that we can continue to expand and maintain our collection of PhET simulations and programs for many years to come.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a12c":"PhET Studio will provide sustaining revenue for the PhET project. This revenue will be directly reinvested to fuel the design, development, and maintenance of free PhET simulations to the benefit of our entire community of educators.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a12d":"Be part of securing PhET’s future, and enjoy the added value of PhET Studio!","phetStudioOverview.faq.a12graphicAltText":"Circular graphic illustrating the cycle of PhET Studio funding the creation of free PhET simulations, which can in turn be used in Studio.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q13":"How can I tell the difference between a PhET sim and a PhET preset?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a13a":"Our familiar PhET simulations have the standard PhET logo in the bottom right corner and are open educational resources, licensed under the Creative Commons 4.0 License (<a {{0}}>CC-BY 4.0</a>). These simulations remain free for classroom use.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a13aGraphicAltText":"Screenshot of a traditional PhET simulation with an arrow pointing out the standard blue and yellow PhET logo in the bottom right corner.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a13b":"PhET presets are crafted using PhET Studio and powered by PhET-iO simulations. PhET-iO simulations are technologically enhanced versions of PhET simulations featuring API capabilities. PhET presets can be identified by their PhET-iO logo and require an active PhET Studio license to make and use.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a13bGraphicAltText":"Screenshot of a PhET preset with an arrow pointing out the gray and white PhET-iO logo in the bottom right corner.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q14":"What is PhET Studio?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a14a":"PhET Studio is a tool that offers educators and education content creators the ability to customize aspects of PhET simulations.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a14b":"Currently, PhET Studio supports modifying the launch state of simulations. In 2026, users will additionally be able to disable and hide some components of simulations. Studio users will play a critical role in guiding the growing feature set of PhET Studio.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q15":"What is a preset?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a15a":"A preset is a customized simulation created using PhET Studio and delivered as a unique URL.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a15b":"Creating, editing, and using presets with your students requires an active PhET Studio license.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q2":"Which sims are compatible with PhET Studio?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a2":"There are currently <a {{0}}>{{1}} simulations</a> available to customize using PhET Studio, with more being added every year","phetStudioOverview.faq.q3":"Do my students need an account to access my presets?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a3":"No. PhET Studio does not allow student logins, and presets are accessed with a URL. Only teachers need PhET Studio accounts to create and share presets.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q4":"How many students can use my presets?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a4a":"Presets don’t require logins to access, so all of your students can use them at the same time.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a4b":"A Classroom Use license only allows for use by your personal students, so each educator who uses presets, including your school colleagues, must have their own PhET Studio license.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q5":"What grade levels does PhET Studio support?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a5a":"The current sims compatible with PhET Studio include grades K-12 and higher education.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a5b":"<a {{0}}>Customizable sims</a> are continually being published.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q6":"Can I import a preset that someone else has created?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a6a":"Yes. A paid PhET Studio license allows you to import a preset that someone else has shared with you. Use the import button on <a {{0}}>My PhET</a> to import a copy of the preset to My Presets.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a6b":"If your preset is imported by someone else, they can see your title but not your notes.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q19":"Can I share my presets with my colleagues?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a19a":"Yes, if they have an active PhET Studio license. <em>Each educator who uses presets, including your school colleagues, must have an active PhET Studio license.</em>","phetStudioOverview.faq.a19b":"Under no circumstances is it permitted to make a collection of presets publicly available. Remember, PhET Studio revenue is critical to securing PhET’s financial sustainability and future operations.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q7":"Will my presets work with my school's LMS?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a7":"Generally, yes. Your presets are links hosted by PhET. They work anywhere you can add a URL, including most learning management systems, like Canvas or Schoology. Keep in mind that some programs may block certain links, so you should always test your preset link in whatever program you wish to use it in.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q8":"What devices are compatible with PhET Studio?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a8":"PhET Studio is web-based, so you can access it from any device with an internet connection. For the best experience, we recommend using a laptop or desktop computer. The Studio interface is designed for larger screens, making it easy to navigate and customize your presets.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q9":"What devices are compatible with presets?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a9":"PhET presets are web-based, so they can be accessed from any device with an internet connection. Presets run in a browser, just like simulations. Read the full system requirements for simulations in our <a {{0}}>Help Center</a>. Presets are not currently supported within the PhET app.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q16":"Can presets be downloaded or accessed offline?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a16":"Presets cannot be downloaded or accessed offline. An internet connection is required to view presets via their unique URL and to edit them in PhET Studio.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q17":"How quickly will students see changes to my presets?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a17":"Presets may take up to 30 seconds to reflect changes saved in PhET Studio. Changes will only appear after a preset has been reloaded.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q18":"What are the terms of service?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a18":"PhET Premium for Classroom Use Terms of Service","phetStudioOverview.faq.q20":"How do I purchase PhET Studio?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a20a":"To create a new PhET Studio license, you must have a PhET account. You can choose to pay immediately using a credit/debit card, or create a quote to share with your purchasing department. Paying a quote or invoice does not require a PhET account.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a20b":"The user who creates the license will automatically be a license admin. Once a license is active, an admin can invite other users to be admins, editors, or both.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q21":"What methods can I use to purchase PhET Studio?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a21":"PhET Studio licenses can be purchased with a credit/debit card or eCheck (ACH) at the time of license creation or by creating a quote first. To pay with a purchase order (PO), email <a {{0}}>phet-studio@colorado.edu</a>.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q22":"What is the purchase agreement?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a22":"PhET Premium for Classroom Use License Purchase Agreement","phetStudioOverview.faq.q23":"My purchase is tax-exempt. What should I do?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a23":"When you complete your purchase, there will be an opportunity to upload a PDF verifying your tax-exemption status. This PDF is often located on your purchase order or provided to you by your purchasing department.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q24":"Where can I find PhET’s W9?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a24":"PhET Interactive Simulations is a part of the University of Colorado Boulder’s Venture Partners organization, and thus uses the <a {{0}}>W9 for Venture Partners</a>.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q25":"Is PhET the “sole source” for PhET Studio?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a25":"Yes, PhET is the only place where you can purchase access to PhET Studio. Learn more in our <a {{0}}>Sole Source Letter<a>.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q26":"Does PhET offer a VPAT or ACR for PhET Studio?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a26":"Yes, PhET offers a combined ACR-VPAT (Accessibility Conformance Report/Voluntary Product Accessibility Template) for PhET Studio and the PhET sims found within PhET Studio. To get a copy of this ACR/VPAT, please email us at <a {{0}}>phet-studio@colorado.edu</a>.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q27":"When will my favorite sim be added to PhET Studio?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a27":"We are working hard to make every sim available in PhET Studio. Adding a sim to PhET Studio is more than just checking a box or writing a line of code, as each customizable sim is a unique version of our standard PhET sims. Allowing a sim to be customizable can take many months, so we are starting with our most popular sims. If there’s a sim you’re waiting for, be sure to let us know using the <a {{0}}>Feedback Form</a>.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q28":"Are PhET Studio sims licensed under CC-BY?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a28":"No. PhET Studio simulations require a license to use them in any capacity. Usage without a license, both in non-commercial and commercial context, is strictly forbidden and may result in legal action.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q29":"Do you support licenses for non-classroom users?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a29":"Yes. Curriculum and commercial licenses are coming soon. If you are interested in other licensing options, please contact our sales team at <a {{0}}>phet-studio@colorado.edu</a>.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q30":"I purchased a license for PhET Studio on the website. Can I use these presets in my commercial product?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a30":"No. PhET Studio licenses purchased through the website are for single classroom, educational, non-commercial use only. If you plan on distributing your presets to other teachers through a shared curriculum, a non-commercial product, or a commercial product, you will need a different license. To get started, reach out to our sales team at <a {{0}}>phet-studio@colorado.edu</a>.","phetStudioOverview.faq.q31":"How do I know if my purchase is tax-exempt?","phetStudioOverview.faq.a31a":"The following is not intended to serve as tax advice. For specific information about your scenario, speak with the purchasing department in your school or district.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a31b":"In general:","phetStudioOverview.faq.a31c":"If you’re purchasing with a Personal Credit Card, your purchase is not tax-exempt.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a31d":"If you’re purchasing with a School or Company Credit Card, the person who gave you the card would have a tax-exempt card or statement that goes with that card.","phetStudioOverview.faq.a31e":"If you’re purchasing with a School or Company Purchase Order (PO), you’ll generally find a tax-exempt statement at the bottom of the purchase order near the purchase total.","phetStudioOverview.faq.dontSeeYourQuestion":"Don't see your question?","phetStudioOverview.faq.contactStudioSupport":"Contact our Studio Support Team at <a {{0}}>phet-studio@colorado.edu</a> or submit your feedback using our <a {{1}}>Feedback Form</a>."}}},features:{"PhetStudioOverviewFeaturesPanel.tsx":function(e,t,n){let i,o,a,r,s,l,c,u,m,d,p;n.export({PhetStudioOverviewFeaturesPanel:()=>h},!0),n.link("react",{default(e){i=e}},0),n.link("../../../../../../api/strings/useStrings",{useStrings(e){o=e}},1),n.link("./phetStudioOverviewFeaturesPanelStrings.json",{default(e){a=e}},2),n.link("../../../../../components/phetText/PhetText",{H2(e){r=e},P(e){s=e}},3),n.link("../../../../../../api/data/constants",