udents away from school, especially those who do not have connections at home.","deibInStemEd.programs.quote2":"Our community is in a rural setting where, thanks to COVID, it was discovered that some areas aren't within reach for any internet service. I feel having the PhET apps downloaded onto student devices will allow for students to have better engagement in the lesson and less frustration with loading issues.","deibInStemEd.programs.whereWeWork":"Where we work","deibInStemEd.programs.whereWeWorkDescription":"The program has provided mobile app access to {{number_of_students}} students across urban, rural, and suburban contexts.","deibInStemEd.programs.whoWeWorkWith":"Who we work with","deibInStemEd.programs.whoWeWorkWithDescription1":"This program supports K-12 schools that are eligible for Title 1 funds or the Community Eligibility Provision.","deibInStemEd.programs.whoWeWorkWithDescription2":"In line with our DEIB commitments, PhET aims to serve a diverse student population.","deibInStemEd.programs.howToGetInvolved":"How to get involved","deibInStemEd.programs.howToGetInvolvedDescription1":"Contact us to learn more about your school’s eligibility: <a {{0}}>phet4schools@colorado.edu</a>","deibInStemEd.programs.howToGetInvolvedDescription2":"If your school is not eligible for this program, please consider requesting a quote on our <a {{0}}>Apps for Schools</a> page.","deibInStemEd.programs.suburban":"Suburban","deibInStemEd.programs.rural":"Rural","deibInStemEd.programs.urban":"Urban","deibInStemEd.programs.highIncome":"High Income","deibInStemEd.programs.mediumIncome":"Medium Income","deibInStemEd.programs.lowIncome":"Low Income","deibInStemEd.programs.veryLowIncome":"Very Low Income","deibInStemEd.programs.black":"Black","deibInStemEd.programs.mixed":"Mixed","deibInStemEd.programs.asian":"Asian","deibInStemEd.programs.hawaiianPacificIslander":"Hawaiian/Pacific Islander","deibInStemEd.programs.americanIndian":"American Indian","deibInStemEd.programs.unknown":"