and programs are equity-aligned. PhET is actively monitoring the impact, feasibility, priority, and activity status of each of the following recommendations:","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendationsHeader":"Recommendations","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list1.header":"Recommendation #1: Multi-Platform Access","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list1.description":"All simulations should be updated to HTML5, and their performance should be tested against as many devices as reasonably possible, integrating Pinch-to-Zoom and double-tap to zoom into all simulations to ensure mobile accessibility.","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list2.header":"Recommendation #2: Multi-Content Area Access","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list2.description":"Simulations should provide wide and equal coverage of all math and science content areas.","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list3.header":"Recommendation #3: Integrated Content Area Access","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list3.description":"There should be many simulations developed to demonstrate cross-curricular connections among science, technology, engineering, and mathematics. Integration may occur within the simulation or its supporting resources.","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list4.header":"Recommendation #4: Multiple Grade Level Access","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list4.description":"There should be simulations with wide and equal coverage of all K-16 grade levels. When possible, simulations should allow for the choice of complexity levels through sim screens and customization. Sim-based teacher supports, such as Teacher Tips, should emphasize spiraling skill and knowledge levels, and how the sim can be used across grade levels.","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list5.header":"Recommendation #5: Diversified Character Sets","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list5.description":"Include fully diversified character sets and hand images, including options to localize sets.","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list6.header":"Recommendation #6: Inclusive Features","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list6.description":"The full suite of PhET simulations should meet <a {{href}}>web content accessibility guidelines</a>. All simulations should include relevant inclusive features (alternative input, sound and sonification, interactive description in English, pan and zoom, and voicing in English and local library languages).","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list7.header":"Recommendation #7: Translation Features","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list7.description":"Translation features should be available within simulations for all <a {{href}}>ISO-639</a> languages and be easy for users to find. Ideally, translated materials should be available for introductory videos and activities (ideally, including dual language options on closed captions).","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list8.header":"Recommendation #8: Past and Present Contributions","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list8.description":"All simulations should include resources for learning about the past and present contributions of diverse sets of individuals to the topic. Updates once every 5-10 years.","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list9.header":"Recommendation #9: Career Connections","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list9.description":"All simulations should include resources for learning about careers related to the topic. Updates once every 5-10 years.","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list10.header":"Recommendation #10: Real-World Applications","deib-in-stem-ed.strategy.recommendation.list10.description":"All simulations should include resources and embedded examples of real-world scenarios or applications of concepts. Simulations provide information about “manipulatives ideas” for hands-on activities."}}},"DeibInStemEdRoutes.tsx":function(e,t,n){let i,o,a,r,s,l,c,u,m,d,p,h,