rldwide to advance knowledge about teaching, learning, and assessment.","licensing.researchWithPhet.description2.item0":"Researchers are encouraged to use PhET simulations from <a {{0}}>https://phet.colorado.edu</a> in their work. These sims are openly licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 license (<a {{1}}>CC BY 4.0</a>). No further permission is necessary to use the simulations in research provided two steps are followed:","licensing.researchWithPhet.description2.item1":"Include proper attribution when a simulation, or any derivative work (e.g. screenshot or video), appears in any education materials, presentations, journal articles, websites, or other channels you may use to distribute your work. Example attribution:","licensing.researchWithPhet.description2.item2":"Simulation by PhET Interactive Simulations, University of Colorado Boulder, licensed under <a {{0}}>CC-BY-4.0</a> (<a {{1}}>https://phet.colorado.edu</a>).","licensing.researchWithPhet.description2.item3":"After you complete your research, share your results with us. Please <a {{0}}>complete this form</a> for each article you publish.","licensing.researchWithPhet.description3":"Researchers interested in customizing simulations or collecting back-end data for use in learning engineering or learning analytics research may be interested in PhET’s interoperable simulations, our PhET-iO simulations. <a {{0}}>Learn more about PhET-iO</a>.","licensing.researchWithPhet.description4":"Education researchers in Africa are invited to participate in <a {{0}}>the webinar series being organized for the Mastercard Foundation</a>.","licensing.teacherSubmittedActivities.header":"Teacher-Submitted Activities","licensing.teacherSubmittedActivities.description1.item0":"A wide variety of <a {{0}}>teaching activities</a> have been contributed by the PhET team and its user community, and are available for you to adapt and use in your classroom. If an activity is marked as a contribution from the PhET team (as indicated by the presence of a PhET logo in the author field), it has been posted as a <a {{1}}>CC-BY</a> resource. For other activities, please contact the submitting author to affirm your use under a CC-BY license. The following attribution is required to share or redistribute CC-BY activities or adapted activities:","licensing.teacherSubmittedActivities.description1.item1":"Activity by [author] licensed under <a {{0}}>CC-BY-4.0</a> ([link to activity page]). <br/>OR","licensing.teacherSubmittedActivities.description1.item2":"This activity has been adapted from an activity by [author] licensed under <a {{0}}>CC-BY-4.0</a> ([link to original activity page]).","licensing.trademarks.header":"Use of PhET Name and Logo (beyond attribution)","licensing.trademarks.description1":"The PhET name and logo are registered trademarks of The Regents of the University of Colorado.","licensing.trademarks.description2":"Use of the PhET name and/or PhET logo for promotional, marketing, or advertising purposes requires a license agreement, and is included as part of our low-cost Basic Partnership. Learn more about our <a {{0}}>Partnership Program</a>.","licensing.phet-io.header":"PhET-iO Simulations","licensing.phet-io.description1":"PhET’s interoperable sims provide enhanced capabilities for interoperability with a wide variety of educational technology, including customization, streaming output data, and versatile API control. PhET-iO sims are a licensed product. <a {{0}}>Learn more about PhET-iO</a>.","licensing.sourceCode.header":"PhET Source Code","licensing.sourceCode.description1":"Most <a {{0}}>PhET simulation source code</a> is available under an open source license – either MIT or GPL. PhET-iO source code is not openly licensed.","licensing.agreements.header":"Full Text Agreements","licensing.agreements.html5":"HTML5 Software Agreement","licensing.agreements.javaFlash":"Java/Flash Software Agreement","licensing.agreements.activityContribution":"Activity Contribution Agreemen